WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.856
The checklist for any guarded route.

2
00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:05.272
Write down what you are guarding against before you pick a guard.

3
00:00:05.552 --> 00:00:12.400
Run deterministic checks (size, format, rate, PII, obvious injection strings) on every request.

4
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:20.168
Choose a model-based classifier with your own labeled data, constrain its output to an enum, and feed it redacted text.

5
00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:27.979
Handle refusals as responses: discard partial output, reset the turn or fall back, and chart the refusal rate.

6
00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:35.171
Validate output against facts you control: schema, citations, canary, the user’s own data, your domain list.

7
00:00:35.451 --> 00:00:44.667
Put every guard on the ledger with its error rates, added latency, and cost, and keep the expensive ones off the critical path unless the risk demands it.

8
00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:52.861
Log every decision with its reason, so the next lesson’s threat model and the last lesson’s incident response have data to work with.
